cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "BraggTrack"
type: software
version: 0.5.1
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/BASE-Laboratory/BraggTrack"
url: "https://github.com/BASE-Laboratory/BraggTrack"
abstract: >-
  4D Bragg reflection segmentation, trajectory tracking, kinematic strain
  extraction, split/merge lineage resolution, operando electrochemistry
  synchronization, and online autonomous Dark-Field X-ray Microscopy (DFXM)
  target selection for operando X-ray diffraction. BraggTrack segments Bragg
  reflections above sCMOS read-noise pedestals, links trajectories and
  intensity-conserved split/merge lineage with analytical Poisson uncertainties
  using classical reciprocal-space geometry, optimal transport, collective slab
  drift registration, and optional vision-transformer descriptors, and exports
  ImageD11, NeXus HDF5, BLISS zoom triggers, and interactive HTML 4D reports.
keywords:
  - X-ray diffraction
  - dark-field X-ray microscopy
  - operando crystallography
  - autonomous experiments
  - 3D segmentation
  - object tracking
  - grain fracture
  - synchrotron
  - materials science
  - Python
authors:
  - family-names: "Le Houx"
    given-names: "James"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1576-0673"
    affiliation: "BASE Laboratory, School of Engineering, University of Greenwich"
